  "section": "observe",
  "title": "Focus on Havana",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Ninety hours in Havana. Outfitted with my new E-M5 Mark II coupled with a pro-grade 12-40mm f2.8 lens, I tagged behind my partner Dee and nephew Kris, who would rather tackle the streets of the Cuban capital than unwind at a resort in Varadero.",
      "style": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Words alone could never describe the atmosphere of the city and the dynamics of the locals. Therefore I\u2019ll let the images from the Olympus with its nifty bells and whistles do most of the talking.",
      "style": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Landmarks and Landscapes",
      "style": ""
